-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- RECONSIDERATION AND APPEAL (regulations 74 to 74.4).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 722 to 740.
--
-- Who may ask for a reconsideration or appeal for a person who cannot manage their affairs (74); what a request for
-- reconsideration sets out, and when the Minister may allow a longer period than the Act gives (74.1); how a notification of
-- an appealable decision is given (74.2). Regulations 74.3 and 74.4 are repealed.
-- The period the Act gives (90 days, section 81(1), piece cp5) is not among the texts this encoding reads: whether a request is
-- late is taken as the request's date and the date of the notice, and the 365-day period of 74.1(4)(a) is worked out here.
-- The Minister's satisfactions are BOOLEAN inputs named for them.

§ `Part V -- Reconsideration and appeal (regulations 74 to 74.2)`

§§ `Regulation 74 -- on behalf of a person incapable of managing their affairs`

-- src:723 | 74 If the Minister or the Social Security Tribunal established under section 44 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act is satisfied, on being presented with medical certificates or other written statements, that a person, by reason of infirmity, illness, insanity or other cause, is incapable of managing their affairs, a request for a reconsideration under subsection 81(1) or (1.1) of the Act or an appeal under section 82 of the Act or section 55 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act may be made on the person’s behalf by another person or an agency if that other person or agency is authorized by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage the person’s affairs or, if it appears to the Minister or the Social Security Tribunal that there is no other person or agency so authorized, if that other person or agency is considered to be qualified to do so by the Minister or the Social Security Tribunal, as the case may be.
@ref Reg 74 (src:723)
GIVEN `the Minister or the Social Security Tribunal is satisfied, on medical certificates or other written statements, that the person is incapable of managing their affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person or agency is authorized by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage the person's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Minister or the Social Security Tribunal that there is no other person or agency so authorized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person or agency is considered to be qualified to do so by the Minister or the Social Security Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 74 — a request for reconsideration or an appeal may be made on behalf of a person incapable of managing their affairs`
    `the Minister or the Social Security Tribunal is satisfied, on medical certificates or other written statements, that the person is incapable of managing their affairs`
    `the other person or agency is authorized by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage the person's affairs`
    `it appears to the Minister or the Social Security Tribunal that there is no other person or agency so authorized`
    `the other person or agency is considered to be qualified to do so by the Minister or the Social Security Tribunal` MEANS
    `the Minister or the Social Security Tribunal is satisfied, on medical certificates or other written statements, that the person is incapable of managing their affairs`
        AND (    `the other person or agency is authorized by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage the person's affairs`
              OR (    `it appears to the Minister or the Social Security Tribunal that there is no other person or agency so authorized`
                  AND `the other person or agency is considered to be qualified to do so by the Minister or the Social Security Tribunal`))

§§ `Regulation 74.1 -- the request for reconsideration`

-- src:726 | 74.1 (1) A request for a reconsideration under subsection 81(1) or (1.1) of the Act shall be made in writing to the Minister and shall set out
-- src:727 | (a) the name, address and Social Insurance Number of the contributor;
-- src:728 | (b) if the person making the request for the reconsideration is not the contributor, that person’s name and address and their relationship to the contributor; and
-- src:729 | (c) the grounds for the request for the reconsideration and a statement of the facts that form the basis of that request.
@ref Reg 74.1(1) (src:726-729)
GIVEN `the person making the request is not the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of a request for reconsideration under regulation 74.1(1)`
`reg 74.1(1) — the items the request has to set out` `the person making the request is not the contributor` MEANS
    append
        (LIST `reg 74.1(1)(a) — the name, address and Social Insurance Number of the contributor`)
        (append
            (IF `the person making the request is not the contributor`
             THEN LIST `reg 74.1(1)(b) — where the person making the request is not the contributor, that person's name and address and relationship to the contributor`
             ELSE EMPTY)
            (LIST `reg 74.1(1)(c) — the grounds for the request and a statement of the facts that form the basis of it`))

@ref Reg 74.1(1) (src:726-729)
GIVEN `the person making the request is not the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the items already set out` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of a request for reconsideration under regulation 74.1(1)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of a request for reconsideration under regulation 74.1(1)`
`reg 74.1(1) — the items the request still has to set out` `the person making the request is not the contributor` `the items already set out` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN item YIELD NOT (elem item `the items already set out`))
        (`reg 74.1(1) — the items the request has to set out` `the person making the request is not the contributor`)

@ref Reg 74.1(1) (src:726)
GIVEN `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 74.1(1) — a request for reconsideration is made as the Regulations require` `the request is made in writing to the Minister` MEANS
    `the request is made in writing to the Minister`

-- src:730 | (2) If it appears to the Minister that the person making the request for a reconsideration has failed to provide information in accordance with any of the requirements of paragraphs (1)(a) to (c) — or has failed to provide sufficient information to allow the Minister to determine if there are circumstances that allow for a longer period in which to make the request — the Minister may take any steps to obtain the information that is necessary to rectify the failure.
@ref Reg 74.1(2) (src:730)
GIVEN `it appears to the Minister that the person making the request has failed to provide information in accordance with paragraphs (1)(a) to (c) or sufficient information to allow the Minister to determine if there are circumstances that allow a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 74.1(2) — the Minister may take any steps to obtain the information that is necessary to rectify the failure`
    `it appears to the Minister that the person making the request has failed to provide information in accordance with paragraphs (1)(a) to (c) or sufficient information to allow the Minister to determine if there are circumstances that allow a longer period` MEANS
    `it appears to the Minister that the person making the request has failed to provide information in accordance with paragraphs (1)(a) to (c) or sufficient information to allow the Minister to determine if there are circumstances that allow a longer period`

-- 74.1(4)(a): "the 365-day period after the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination".
-- src:731 | (3) For the purposes of subsections 81(1) and (1.1) of the Act and subject to subsection (4), the Minister may allow a longer period to make a request for reconsideration of a decision or determination if the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for requesting a longer period and the person has demonstrated a continuing intention to request a reconsideration.
-- src:732 | (4) The Minister must also be satisfied that the request for reconsideration has a reasonable chance of success, and that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period to make the request, if the request for reconsideration
-- src:733 | (a) is made after the 365-day period after the day on which the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination;
-- src:734 | (b) is made by a person who has applied again for the same benefit; or
-- src:735 | (c) is made by a person who has requested the Minister to rescind or amend a decision under subsection 81(3) of the Act.
@ref Reg 74.1(4) (src:733)
GIVEN `the day the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 74.1(4)(a) — the last day of the 365-day period after the notification` `the day the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the day the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 365)

@ref Reg 74.1(4) (src:732-735)
GIVEN `the day the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination` IS A DATE
      `the date the request for reconsideration is made` IS A DATE
      `the request is made by a person who has applied again for the same benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made by a person who has requested the Minister to rescind or amend a decision under subsection 81(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 81(3) (piece cp5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 74.1(4) — the Minister must also be satisfied of a reasonable chance of success and no prejudice`
    `the day the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination`
    `the date the request for reconsideration is made`
    `the request is made by a person who has applied again for the same benefit`
    `the request is made by a person who has requested the Minister to rescind or amend a decision under subsection 81(3) of the Act` MEANS
    `the date the request for reconsideration is made` GREATER THAN
        (`reg 74.1(4)(a) — the last day of the 365-day period after the notification` `the day the person is notified in writing of the decision or determination`)
        OR `the request is made by a person who has applied again for the same benefit`
        OR `the request is made by a person who has requested the Minister to rescind or amend a decision under subsection 81(3) of the Act`

@ref Reg 74.1(3) (src:731)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for requesting a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has demonstrated a continuing intention to request a reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (4) applies to the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the request has a reasonable chance of success` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 74.1(3) — the Minister may allow a longer period to make a request for reconsideration`
    `the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for requesting a longer period`
    `the person has demonstrated a continuing intention to request a reconsideration`
    `subsection (4) applies to the request`
    `the Minister is satisfied that the request has a reasonable chance of success`
    `the Minister is satisfied that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period` MEANS
    `the Minister is satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for requesting a longer period`
        AND `the person has demonstrated a continuing intention to request a reconsideration`
        AND ((NOT `subsection (4) applies to the request`)
             OR (    `the Minister is satisfied that the request has a reasonable chance of success`
                 AND `the Minister is satisfied that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period`))

§§ `Regulation 74.2 -- notification of an appealable decision`

-- src:738 | 74.2 A notification referred to in subsection 81(1) or (1.1) of the Act must be in writing and sent by the Minister.
@ref Reg 74.2 (src:738)
GIVEN `the notification is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification is sent by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 74.2 — a notification referred to in subsection 81(1) or (1.1) of the Act is given as the Regulations require`
    `the notification is in writing` `the notification is sent by the Minister` MEANS
    `the notification is in writing` AND `the notification is sent by the Minister`
